# Telecom operator domain

This workspace builds **apps and websites for telecom operators** (MNOs/MVNOs) and their subscribers.

- Do **not** treat work as a generic consumer/SaaS app
- Follow telecom industry language and journey conventions (SIM/eSIM activation, MSISDN login, plans/packs, self-care, prepaid/postpaid when relevant)
- Keep PRDs **brandless / tenant-agnostic** in wording by default (do not invent brand Non-Goals)
- Use **everyday product language** (user, button, logged in — not jargon)
- Full shared context: `.cursor/skills/shared/telecom-domain.md` and `.cursor/skills/shared/general-context.md` (product-wide rules, e.g. generic error for API failure or unhandled error code — defined once, not repeated in PRDs)
- **PRD folders:** `prebuilt_prds/` = catalog prebuilts (current focus, e.g. `LF-*`); `project_prds/` = project/tenant PRDs (later). `generate-prd` supports both; default target today is **prebuilt**.
- **Skills:** users type parent names only at the start of the message: `generate-prd`, `design-prd-consistency`, `publish-prd`, `review-prd`, `relate-prds`, `api-mapping` — children are internal (see `.cursor/skills/shared/invocation.md`)
- **API mapping:** only via `api-mapping` when asked. From spec: operation YAML. From PRD + operation YAML: compare first — match → mapping YAML, §7, and Header API Spec (link to that YAML); mismatch → raise, write nothing (do not attach). Do not auto-run after `generate-prd`.
- **Publish:** only via `publish-prd` when asked — never auto-offer after `generate-prd`. With no path, walks every AIDR PRD under `prebuilt_prds/` against Confluence, one by one. Asks once whether to run `review-prd`; if the user says no, skip review for the whole run and fill Header Figma / API Spec `TBD` with `N / A` (do not ask again). Blocks on product `TBD` or empty required sections (`N / A` is accepted; Header Confluence `TBD` is filled on publish; Header Jira `—` / `TBD` is left as-is). Compares to Confluence first (page-level and inline comments; **Resolve** closes the comment on Confluence). If Change Log or Last updated differs, uses the most latest without asking. Writes local to Confluence only when still different; always fills Header → Confluence with this PRD’s page URL on local and wiki; does not fill Header → Jira from the AIDR board; then commits those PRDs and pushes if origin exists. Does not use `confluence-mapping.json`. Does not publish from git.
